# Production build config — baked into the hosted bundle at build time.
# A bare 'npm run build' without these ships a bundle that dials localhost
# and has no space configured (2026-07-16 incident). Verify after building:
#   grep -o 'localhost:[0-9]*' dist/assets/*.js | sort -u              # must be EMPTY
#   grep -c 'swimchain.io/rpc' dist/assets/index-*.js                  # must be >=1
#   grep -c 'sp1qqz7zj8gawkmy3ye7vyxudvalfmqpxt7ue' dist/assets/index-*.js
#   grep -c '0530df507ad26a2ee6d0c61ef1e37e4e08abae087c1755467d98e3435ecd2984' dist/assets/index-*.js
#
# NOTE on '127.0.0.1': the built bundle WILL contain this literal string, and
# that is expected — it is @swimchain/react's LOCAL_TESTNET dev constant,
# baked into every client that imports the shared RPC hook (confirmed present
# in the live production reef bundle too, 2026-07-25). It is not a leaked
# fallback: chips-client/src/lib/host.ts's assertConfigured() throws at
# startup if VITE_CHIPS_RPC or VITE_CHIPS_SPACE is empty, so a misconfigured
# build refuses to run rather than quietly dialling localhost. Do NOT
# resurrect a '127.0.0.1 must be empty' gate on this string — it fails
# every shipping client, not just a broken one. localhost:PORT (with an
# actual port number) is the real signal and must stay empty.
VITE_CHIPS_RPC=https://swimchain.io/rpc
VITE_CHIPS_SPACE=sp1qqz7zj8gawkmy3ye7vyxudvalfmqpxt7ue
# Game onboarding sponsor: the ALWAYS-ONLINE node that auto-approves new
# players. MUST be a running sponsor — defaulting to the genesis root (an
# offline identity) is what hung onboarding on 2026-07-18. This is the bot
# identity on 165.22.47.107 (always-on, already approving). Client is pinned
# strictly to this sponsor.
VITE_GAME_SPONSOR=0530df507ad26a2ee6d0c61ef1e37e4e08abae087c1755467d98e3435ecd2984
